# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. Never commit a filled-in copy.
#
# Both values are read on the SERVER only. Neither is prefixed `NEXT_PUBLIC_`,
# and neither should ever be — that would inline them into the browser bundle.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SFLUV_API_BASE_URL — base URL of the SFLuv backend.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production:  https://api.sfluv.org
# Local:       http://localhost:8080
#
# UNSET IN DEVELOPMENT: the volunteer pages serve local sample events and stub
# out signups, so the site is workable without a backend.
#
# UNSET IN PRODUCTION: sample data is deliberately NOT served. Event pages
# degrade to "temporarily unavailable" and signups return an error, because
# advertising events that do not exist — or telling someone they are signed up
# when nothing was recorded — is worse than an outage. Set this in every
# deployed environment.
SFLUV_API_BASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SFLUV_VOLUNTEER_PROXY_KEY — shared secret for signup rate limiting.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anonymous signups are proxied through our own route handler, so every request
# reaches the API from one egress IP. Left alone, the API's per-IP rate limit
# would put all of sfluv.org in a single bucket.
#
# We therefore forward the visitor's real IP as `X-Forwarded-For` — but that
# header is trivially forged by anyone posting to the API directly, so the API
# only trusts it when accompanied by this secret. It authenticates the CLAIM
# ABOUT THE IP, not the signup itself; signups stay public and anonymous.
#
# Must match `VOLUNTEER_PROXY_KEY` on the backend (note the different name).
#
# UNSET: signups still work. The API falls back to the socket IP, so web
# signups share one rate-limit bucket — degraded, not broken.
#
# Generate with:  openssl rand -hex 32
SFLUV_VOLUNTEER_PROXY_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SFLUV_USE_FIXTURES — force local sample data on. Optional.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `pnpm dev` already uses fixtures when SFLUV_API_BASE_URL is unset. This flag
# additionally allows a PRODUCTION build (`pnpm build && pnpm start`) to run
# against them, which is useful for verifying the real build locally.
#
# Never set this in a deployed environment.
# SFLUV_USE_FIXTURES=1
